  "methodology": "Every library is measured the same way: an entry re-exporting what the module's bench file in its __benches__ folder names, bundled and minified by esbuild with react and react-dom external, then gzipped. gentleduck is the whole dist module; Radix, Base UI, Ark UI, cmdk, input-otp and vaul are their whole package or subpath; React Aria, Headless UI and react-day-picker, which ship one entry for everything, are the named parts a component draws. A total is one bundle of every part it covers, so shared code counts once: gentleduck's own row is the whole library, and each other library's row carries gentleduckKB, gentleduck over the same components. The calendar's gentleduck figure includes the NativeAdapter it needs.",
